# Search filter

Add filters only to a substantial catalogue, and keep the result count, the list and the no-match message in step. Choose facets that reflect the task, such as area, domain or availability. A short list that is easy to scan does not need a filter panel.

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## Share the filtering contract

The [search input](../../components/search-input.html) owns the query field. This pattern owns how query, facets and results work together. The [finder](../frontend-templates/finder.html) composes this contract for a named collection, and its child pages do not define new filter rules.

In these examples, all query words must match a record, values selected within the Area facet are alternatives, and the query combines with the selected facet. Apply and Clear work on the same fixed record set. Without JavaScript, show the records and keep submission disabled rather than sending the query to the current page. A real implementation needs its own permitted dataset, loading state and error behaviour.

## When to use it

Use filters for a large device, automation or document catalogue, for example narrowing sample records to the Kitchen. Keep selected criteria visible and easy to clear.

## Structure and behaviour

Group related choices with a fieldset and legend. Keep search, filters and results in a logical order. A mobile disclosure can hold the same controls, with a link back to results. Native Home Assistant owns entity visibility and real filtering. A documentation specimen is not an entity registry.

## Home Assistant boundary

Automatic refresh must not move focus away from the changed filter. Say when results are loading and when no records match. Keep meaningful query state when someone navigates back. These examples apply filters only when the person submits them, and Clear filters restores the fixed dataset. Counts and empty-state messages reflect the visible records. No live entities are queried.

